  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "Es ist ein Ros entsprungen means A rose has sprung up in German. It is a church Christmas song from the 16th century. Its tune was first printed in the Speyer hymnal, in Cologne in 1599, and its composer is unknown. Michael Praetorius set it for four voices in 1609, and his setting spread widely.",
